# Every path serves the app shell, so React Router can read it (#27).
#
# `src/App.tsx` uses BrowserRouter, which means /vocabulary and /journal/<id>
# are real URLs the host is asked for. Without this line a deep link, a reload
# or a bookmark 404s before any JavaScript runs.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser keeps the URL it asked for and is handed
# index.html as the body, which is exactly what the router needs to see.
#
# Read by Netlify and by Cloudflare Pages, both from the published directory,
# which is why it lives in `public/` and ships in the build rather than sitting
# in a host-specific config file.
/*    /index.html    200
